      "parentCompany": null,
      "shortDescription": "Gneuss develops equipment and process technology for polymer extrusion, plastics recycling and polymer-melt treatment. Its portfolio includes extrusion and recycling systems, rotary melt-filtration systems, vacuum technology, process sensors, online viscosity measurement and PET polyreaction equipment.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Gneuss Kunststofftechnik GmbH is a family-owned German engineering company founded in Bad Oeynhausen in 1983. The manufacturer develops systems and components for processing and recycling polymer melts, including complete lines for producing sheet, fibres and pellets.",
        "Its documented portfolio covers OMNI recycling systems, MRS, MRSpure and MDS extrusion systems, rotary melt filters and screen changers, vacuum equipment, process-control technology, pressure and temperature sensors, the VIS online viscometer and JUMP polyreaction equipment. Gneuss supports these technologies through its German headquarters and an international sales and service network."
      ],
